{"duration_api_ms":436535,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"90ee8c22-2aae-4870-8555-1516609fc3ad","total_cost_usd":2.1186850000000006,"usage":{"input_tokens":170,"cache_creation_input_tokens":89138,"cache_read_input_tokens":6586605,"output_tokens":41199,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4954},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":89138,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3016,"cache_read_input_tokens":105780,"cache_creation_input_tokens":382,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":382},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":25117,"outputTokens":1473,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.032482,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":170,"outputTokens":41199,"cacheReadInputTokens":6586605,"cacheCreationInputTokens":89138,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.0862030000000007,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":4954,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":113,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Deployed a 3-node RabbitMQ 4.3.5 cluster (node1/node2/node3, CentOS Stream 10) using the official RabbitMQ Cloudsmith el9 repos. Created a dedicated CA and per-node server certs; rabbitmq.conf enforces listeners.tcp=none / TLS-only AMQP on 5671 with ssl_options.verify=verify_peer and fail_if_no_peer_cert=true, so only clients presenting a certificate issued by this CA are accepted (verified both positive and negative cases at the TLS layer and at the AMQP/pika protocol layer). Management HTTP API (15672) is bound to each node's own cluster IP (not 0.0.0.0-equivalent wildcard reachability) and firewalld restricts 15672/4369/25672 to the 10.100.195.0/24 cluster subnet only, while 5671 stays open for external AMQPS clients. guest user removed; a cluster_admin administrator account created. Ran the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes: captured boot_id + healthy cluster/service state, issued systemd reboot (ack returned pre-disconnect), polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, and verified RabbitMQ active with full 3/3 running nodes and zero network partitions after each restart, only proceeding to the next node once the cluster was fully healthy.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed all 3 nodes (CentOS Stream 10, no prior RabbitMQ/Erlang) and confirmed outbound internet access\",\"Fetched current RabbitMQ el9 Cloudsmith repo/signing-key instructions via WebFetch and applied them to all nodes\",\"Installed erlang + rabbitmq-server + logrotate on node1/node2/node3 in parallel (backgrounded, polled logs to completion)\",\"Set up passwordless inter-node SSH via CLUSTER_SSH_PRIVKEY/PUBKEY and populated /etc/hosts from CLUSTER_HOSTS\",\"Generated a dedicated CA (RabbitMQ Cluster CA) plus per-node server certs (CN/SAN = node name + cluster IP) and a CA-signed client cert, all on node1; distributed CA cert + server cert/key to node2/node3 via scp with correct ownership (root:rabbitmq) and SELinux context (rabbitmq_conf_t)\",\"Generated a shared Erlang cookie and distributed it to all three nodes for clustering\",\"Wrote /etc/rabbitmq/rabbitmq.conf on each node: listeners.tcp=none, TLS-only AMQP on 5671 with verify_peer+fail_if_no_peer_cert, management.tcp.ip bound to each node's own IP, classic_config peer discovery listing all 3 nodes\",\"Enabled rabbitmq_management plugin (offline) on all nodes\",\"Configured firewalld on all nodes: opened 5671/tcp publicly, restricted 15672/4369/25672 to 10.100.195.0/24 via rich rules\",\"Started/enabled rabbitmq-server on all 3 nodes; verified automatic cluster formation (3/3 running, disk nodes, no partitions)\",\"Created cluster_admin administrator user, deleted default guest user\",\"Generated a rogue self-signed cert (not CA-signed) and used openssl s_client plus a Python/pika AMQPS test to prove: CA-signed client cert connects and can publish/consume; rogue cert is rejected with a TLS bad_certificate alert both at handshake and application level\",\"Verified management API reachable (401 auth prompt) from a cluster peer and bound only to the node's own IP, not a wildcard address\",\"Executed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol sequentially on node1, node2, then node3: captured boot_id + cluster health baseline, issued a backgrounded systemd reboot so the ack returned first, polled until SSH/exec responded again, confirmed boot_id changed, and verified RabbitMQ service active with full 3-node cluster and zero partitions before proceeding to the next node\",\"Re-verified TLS accept/reject behavior and firewalld persistence after all restarts completed\",\"Cleaned up temporary test users/queues created for verification\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"RabbitMQ cluster spans node1, node2, node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-95b0fe057e224689\",\"cmd-c520e74986a24b27\",\"cmd-c1f8c61d1b8240ec\",\"cmd-d9b19442803d478b\"],\"summary\":\"cluster_status shows rabbit@node1/node2/node3 as Disk Nodes and Running Nodes with no partitions, both at initial formation and after each restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"AMQP served over TLS using a cluster-created CA\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a521c8cb95d54974\",\"cmd-27f53b76589b4537\",\"cmd-98c68a3447ae4535\",\"cmd-95b0fe057e224689\"],\"summary\":\"CA generated on node1 (openssl req -x509), per-node server certs signed by it, rabbitmq.conf sets listeners.tcp=none and listeners.ssl.default=5671 with ssl_options pointing at the CA/server cert/key; cluster_status listeners show amqp/ssl on 5671 only\"},{\"requirement\":\"Only clients presenting a certificate issued by the cluster CA are accepted\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-15575f2091d941f0\",\"cmd-aca65930c6f649ad\",\"cmd-8be39087b3784319\",\"cmd-25214f131cb84451\",\"cmd-ee49bb4835944f7e\",\"cmd-13079e10a4844284\"],\"summary\":\"CA-signed client cert completes TLS handshake and successfully publishes/consumes an AMQPS message via pika; a self-signed (rogue) cert is rejected with tls_alert bad_certificate both in the RabbitMQ log and as a client-side SSLError, confirmed again after all node restarts\"},{\"requirement\":\"Management interface reachable only from within the cluster\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-98c68a3447ae4535\",\"cmd-e99ecdd466014b5d\",\"cmd-63bcf7fc8f5d4249\",\"cmd-055c1c489d004f4e\"],\"summary\":\"management.tcp.ip bound to each node's own cluster IP (not wildcard), firewalld rich rules restrict 15672/4369/25672 to 10.100.195.0/24, and a request from a cluster peer (node2) reaches the API (401) while firewall config persisted through reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart evidence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ec47006203854fd9\",\"cmd-41f216f2f3144ac4\",\"cmd-25593e1f65164584\",\"cmd-93e97254735b41c1\",\"cmd-c520e74986a24b27\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 4cee4ea8...; reboot ack returned pre-disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to c2073cdd...; rabbitmq-server active/enabled; cluster back to 3/3 running nodes, no partitions\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart evidence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3c735ba4ae8a4759\",\"cmd-602156c4343a4ca4\",\"cmd-defd5a7a45ba4b19\",\"cmd-c1f8c61d1b8240ec\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id a70d7f83...; reboot ack returned pre-disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to 87a7d36b...; rabbitmq-server active and cluster shows 3/3 running nodes, no partitions\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart evidence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3cd94b85eb1f4d66\",\"cmd-cf7e2cd6c85e4d79\",\"cmd-40b30548c6e4478b\",\"cmd-d9b19442803d478b\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 984a7d52...; reboot ack returned pre-disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to 7de934fb...; rabbitmq-server active and cluster shows 3/3 running nodes, no partitions\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a 3-node RabbitMQ 4.3.5 cluster (node1/node2/node3, CentOS Stream 10) using the official RabbitMQ Cloudsmith el9 repos. Created a dedicated CA and per-node server certs; rabbitmq.conf enforces listeners.tcp=none / TLS-only AMQP on 5671 with ssl_options.verify=verify_peer and fail_if_no_peer_cert=true, so only clients presenting a certificate issued by this CA are accepted (verified both positive and negative cases at the TLS layer and at the AMQP/pika protocol layer). Management HTTP API (15672) is bound to each node's own cluster IP (not 0.0.0.0-equivalent wildcard reachability) and firewalld restricts 15672/4369/25672 to the 10.100.195.0/24 cluster subnet only, while 5671 stays open for external AMQPS clients. guest user removed; a cluster_admin administrator account created. Ran the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes: captured boot_id + healthy cluster/service state, issued systemd reboot (ack returned pre-disconnect), polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, and verified RabbitMQ active with full 3/3 running nodes and zero network partitions after each restart, only proceeding to the next node once the cluster was fully healthy.","actions_performed":["Surveyed all 3 nodes (CentOS Stream 10, no prior RabbitMQ/Erlang) and confirmed outbound internet access","Fetched current RabbitMQ el9 Cloudsmith repo/signing-key instructions via WebFetch and applied them to all nodes","Installed erlang + rabbitmq-server + logrotate on node1/node2/node3 in parallel (backgrounded, polled logs to completion)","Set up passwordless inter-node SSH via CLUSTER_SSH_PRIVKEY/PUBKEY and populated /etc/hosts from CLUSTER_HOSTS","Generated a dedicated CA (RabbitMQ Cluster CA) plus per-node server certs (CN/SAN = node name + cluster IP) and a CA-signed client cert, all on node1; distributed CA cert + server cert/key to node2/node3 via scp with correct ownership (root:rabbitmq) and SELinux context (rabbitmq_conf_t)","Generated a shared Erlang cookie and distributed it to all three nodes for clustering","Wrote /etc/rabbitmq/rabbitmq.conf on each node: listeners.tcp=none, TLS-only AMQP on 5671 with verify_peer+fail_if_no_peer_cert, management.tcp.ip bound to each node's own IP, classic_config peer discovery listing all 3 nodes","Enabled rabbitmq_management plugin (offline) on all nodes","Configured firewalld on all nodes: opened 5671/tcp publicly, restricted 15672/4369/25672 to 10.100.195.0/24 via rich rules","Started/enabled rabbitmq-server on all 3 nodes; verified automatic cluster formation (3/3 running, disk nodes, no partitions)","Created cluster_admin administrator user, deleted default guest user","Generated a rogue self-signed cert (not CA-signed) and used openssl s_client plus a Python/pika AMQPS test to prove: CA-signed client cert connects and can publish/consume; rogue cert is rejected with a TLS bad_certificate alert both at handshake and application level","Verified management API reachable (401 auth prompt) from a cluster peer and bound only to the node's own IP, not a wildcard address","Executed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol sequentially on node1, node2, then node3: captured boot_id + cluster health baseline, issued a backgrounded systemd reboot so the ack returned first, polled until SSH/exec responded again, confirmed boot_id changed, and verified RabbitMQ service active with full 3-node cluster and zero partitions before proceeding to the next node","Re-verified TLS accept/reject behavior and firewalld persistence after all restarts completed","Cleaned up temporary test users/queues created for verification"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"RabbitMQ cluster spans node1, node2, node3","command_ids":["cmd-95b0fe057e224689","cmd-c520e74986a24b27","cmd-c1f8c61d1b8240ec","cmd-d9b19442803d478b"],"summary":"cluster_status shows rabbit@node1/node2/node3 as Disk Nodes and Running Nodes with no partitions, both at initial formation and after each restart"},{"requirement":"AMQP served over TLS using a cluster-created CA","command_ids":["cmd-a521c8cb95d54974","cmd-27f53b76589b4537","cmd-98c68a3447ae4535","cmd-95b0fe057e224689"],"summary":"CA generated on node1 (openssl req -x509), per-node server certs signed by it, rabbitmq.conf sets listeners.tcp=none and listeners.ssl.default=5671 with ssl_options pointing at the CA/server cert/key; cluster_status listeners show amqp/ssl on 5671 only"},{"requirement":"Only clients presenting a certificate issued by the cluster CA are accepted","command_ids":["cmd-15575f2091d941f0","cmd-aca65930c6f649ad","cmd-8be39087b3784319","cmd-25214f131cb84451","cmd-ee49bb4835944f7e","cmd-13079e10a4844284"],"summary":"CA-signed client cert completes TLS handshake and successfully publishes/consumes an AMQPS message via pika; a self-signed (rogue) cert is rejected with tls_alert bad_certificate both in the RabbitMQ log and as a client-side SSLError, confirmed again after all node restarts"},{"requirement":"Management interface reachable only from within the cluster","command_ids":["cmd-98c68a3447ae4535","cmd-e99ecdd466014b5d","cmd-63bcf7fc8f5d4249","cmd-055c1c489d004f4e"],"summary":"management.tcp.ip bound to each node's own cluster IP (not wildcard), firewalld rich rules restrict 15672/4369/25672 to 10.100.195.0/24, and a request from a cluster peer (node2) reaches the API (401) while firewall config persisted through reboot"},{"requirement":"node1 restart evidence","command_ids":["cmd-ec47006203854fd9","cmd-41f216f2f3144ac4","cmd-25593e1f65164584","cmd-93e97254735b41c1","cmd-c520e74986a24b27"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 4cee4ea8...; reboot ack returned pre-disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to c2073cdd...; rabbitmq-server active/enabled; cluster back to 3/3 running nodes, no partitions"},{"requirement":"node2 restart evidence","command_ids":["cmd-3c735ba4ae8a4759","cmd-602156c4343a4ca4","cmd-defd5a7a45ba4b19","cmd-c1f8c61d1b8240ec"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id a70d7f83...; reboot ack returned pre-disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to 87a7d36b...; rabbitmq-server active and cluster shows 3/3 running nodes, no partitions"},{"requirement":"node3 restart evidence","command_ids":["cmd-3cd94b85eb1f4d66","cmd-cf7e2cd6c85e4d79","cmd-40b30548c6e4478b","cmd-d9b19442803d478b"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 984a7d52...; reboot ack returned pre-disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to 7de934fb...; rabbitmq-server active and cluster shows 3/3 running nodes, no partitions"}]},"ttft_ms":1469,"type":"result","duration_ms":571970,"uuid":"971465cf-3752-4354-9074-84ad9ad2f005","ttft_stream_ms":854,"time_to_request_ms":49,"first_content_frame_ms":1171,"queued_turn_count":0}
